@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+---
+id: task-001-rental-module-basics
+type: task
+title: "Rental module basics"
+status: approved
+format: 1
+---
+
+# Rental module basics
+
+The booking desk gets a rental module, starting with the basics. It is an in-memory service exported
+from `src/index.ts` as `createRentalService()`.
+
+## Scope
+
+- `addEquipment({ id, kind, dailyPrice })`: `id` is a string, `kind` is `'board'` or `'sail'`,
+  `dailyPrice` is the price of one rental day in integer euro cents.
+- `quote({ itemId, start, end })`: returns `{ itemId, start, end, total }`, the cost of renting the item
+  for the period.
+- `book({ itemId, start, end })`: books the item and returns `{ id, itemId, start, end, total }`, where
+  `id` identifies the booking.
+- `quote` and `book` throw for an unknown item or a period the rules do not allow. `book` also throws
+  when the item is not free for the whole period.
+- Cancellation is out of scope for this task. The cancellation policy comes later.
+
+## Rules (apply to everything the module does)
+
+1. Money is an integer number of euro cents.
+2. Times are UTC, written as ISO-8601 strings.
+3. A booking covers whole days only: a period starts and ends at midnight UTC and ends at the start of
+   the day after its last day.
+4. The same item cannot be booked twice for overlapping periods.
+5. Cancellation policy (for later): a booking cancelled less than 24 hours before its start gets no
+   refund; otherwise the full amount is refunded.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+- AC1: `quote` for `N` whole days returns `N * dailyPrice` as an integer number of cents.
+- AC2: a period that is not whole UTC days, or that ends before or at its start, is rejected by `quote`
+  and `book`.
+- AC3: an unknown `itemId` is rejected by `quote` and `book`.
+- AC4: `book` returns a booking with an `id` and the same `total` that `quote` gives.
+- AC5: `book` of an item already booked for an overlapping period throws; a period that only touches the
+  end of an existing booking (it starts at the end of it) does not overlap and is accepted.
+- AC6: a booking of one item does not block another item for the same period.
+- AC7: no cancellation API is exposed.
+
+## Traceability
+
+Requirements: the five school rules above. Each acceptance criterion maps to one or more tests.
